#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:7
msgid "Bruno Ribeiro"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:17
msgid ""
"Lumen finds Yeelight lights on the local network and lets you turn them on "
"or off, change brightness, set a color or a white temperature, save colors, "
"group lights, run an effect, and set a sleep timer. It is a native GNOME "
"application and does not need a Yeelight account or an internet connection."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:20
msgid ""
"LAN Control has to be enabled for each light in the Yeelight mobile app. "
"Names you choose are stored on this computer and stay attached to the light "
"even if its IP address changes."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:23
msgid ""
"Yeelight is a trademark of its owner. Lumen is an independent project and is "
"not affiliated with Yeelight."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:33
msgid "The light list, with power, brightness, and color controls"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:37
msgid "Lumen in the dark style"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:44
msgid ""
"Lights and groups are on separate pages. A group can have an icon, the sleep "
"timer accepts a custom duration, and each light's menu shows only the "
"controls that light supports."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:49
msgid "Group cards use the same inner padding as light cards."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:54
msgid ""
"The window can stay connected after it is closed, and Toggle All Lights can "
"be bound as a system shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:59
msgid ""
"Adds color temperature, saved colors, groups, effects, a sleep timer, all-on "
"and all-off, adding a light by address, an optional name stored on the bulb, "
"and a Brazilian Portuguese translation."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.bruno_srio.Lumen.metainfo.xml.in:64
msgid ""
"Power, brightness, and color changes are sent to the lights. Names and "
"addresses are remembered between launches."
msgstr ""
